-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/59/Serundeng_Daging.jpg/500px-Serundeng_Daging.jpg","w":500,"h":465,"by":"Gunawan Kartapranata","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Serundeng_Daging.jpg"}},"dish/vatrushka":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/vatrushka","n":"Vatrushka","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Vatrushka is an Eastern European pastry (pirog), characterized by a ring-shape of dough with traditional white cheese Tvorog in the middle, sometimes with the addition of raisins or bits of fruit. The most common size is about 5–10 cm (2–4 in) in diameter, but larger versions also exist. Vatrushkas are typically baked using a sweet yeast bread dough. Savoury varieties are made using unsweetened dough, with onion added to the filling."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-vatrushka"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vatrushka"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Tvorog","ingredient/tvorog"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Olga's Flavor Factory","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"olgasflavorfactory.com","note":"Russian-born home cook Olga's blog, with a dedicated Russian recipes category.","url":"https://www.olgasflavorfactory.com/category/russianrecipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Savas Kitc